 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Depends on the specific algorithm (Greedy Meshing is generally faster for blocky data; Marching Cubes is more expensive for smooth data).
-- **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the voxel data representation (e.g., half-precision density reduces memory usage) [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Extensibility, performance via job systems, separation of concerns.
-- **Limitations:** Requires careful management of job scheduling and buffer synchronization.
+- **Performance:** Jobs are burst-compiled and designed for zero garbage collection, optimizing performance in managed environments like Unity [S1, unofficial].
+- **Memory:** Using half-precision density fields reduces memory usage by 50% (68KB vs 128KB per 32³ chunk) [S1, unofficial].
+- **Scalability:** The architecture supports automatic job scheduling and spatial hashing for chunk management [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-The architecture was introduced in the StraightFour voxel engine project [S1, unofficial]. It allows for the integration of different meshing techniques (greedy meshing, marching cubes) within a unified chunk management system [S1, unofficial].
+The Mesh Plugin Architecture was introduced in the StraightFour voxel engine project to support both generic, terrain, and smooth voxel rendering [S1, unofficial]. It allows for the integration of different meshing techniques (greedy meshing and marching cubes) within a unified pipeline.
 
